To make ESLint ignore all rules for a single line, you can use a comment to disable and re-enable the rules. Here are the steps:

1. **Disable All Rules for a Line:**
   - Use the `/*eslint-disable */` comment at the beginning of the line you want to ignore.
   - Use the `/*eslint-enable */` comment at the end of the line to re-enable the rules.

2. **Example:**
   ```javascript
   /*eslint-disable */
   console.log('This line will not follow any ESLint rules.');
   /*eslint-enable */
   ```

3. **Disabling Specific Rules:**
   - If you want to disable specific rules, you can specify them within the comment.
   - For example, to disable the `no-console` rule:
     ```javascript
     /*eslint-disable no-console */
     console.log('This line will not follow the no-console rule.');
     /*eslint-enable */
     ```

